  "review_decisions": [
    "Local existence uses a self-map ball and a time-uniform state Lipschitz bound; the fixed-point theorem now explicitly requires a nonempty space.",
    "The Peano-Baker product order and integration-simplex factorial are explicit; scalar integrating factors are not silently transferred to noncommuting matrices.",
    "Continuation requires compact containment in the equation domain, not only a bounded state.",
    "Centrifugal instability and viscous Gaussian envelopes belong to B07; the ODE machinery supporting them is supplied here.",
    "The existing exponential series is extended to complex inputs, with real-order properties kept in a separate real-restriction section.",
    "Real analyticity, holomorphic dependence, formal radial coefficients and their convergent realization are distinct statements.",
    "Common domains and complex bounds are explicit hypotheses; real-axis bounds do not substitute for them.",
    "The two-index coefficient construction uses arbitrary radii R and rho; its completeness, product constant 256, integration ratios, mixed derivative bound and realization radius are derived explicitly.",
    "The operator inverse is justified from summable powers with factorial bounds, without assuming its one-step norm is small.",
    "The three pre-existing subject-index label findings from earlier batches remain unrelated baseline findings."
  ],
